    <briefdescription>
<para>Evaluates filter predicates against a file-level index to determine file eligibility. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_index_reader" kindref="compound">FileIndexReader</ref></computeroutput> implements the <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_function_visitor" kindref="compound">FunctionVisitor</ref></computeroutput> interface specialized to produce <computeroutput>std::shared_ptr&lt;<ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_index_result" kindref="compound">FileIndexResult</ref>&gt;</computeroutput> objects. It reads pre-built file-level index data (e.g., bitmap, bsi or bloom filters) from index file and evaluates whether a given data file may contain rows matching a specific predicate. <simplesect kind="note"><para>Callers of <computeroutput>Visit*</computeroutput> for DECIMAL fields must ensure each literal&apos;s scale matches the scale of the indexed data; otherwise, index filtering results may be incorrect. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
